  "creator": "alphaxmachine",
  "title": "Glove80 macOS — host Colemak + symbols",
  "notes": "macOS programming layout for standard OS-side Colemak. Base letters send QWERTY keycodes; Command and Control follow the macOS factory variant.\n\nThumb trial: left upper Shift position holds Symbols (1); left Backspace is plain and repeats when held; right Enter taps Enter / holds Command; tap left thumb Tab / hold Numbers (5); tap right Space / hold Navigation (4). Dedicated left Layer also holds Symbols. Within typing layers, thumb Backspace, Tab, and Space are plain keypresses. Hold Navigation N for repeating Backspace.\n\nSymbols replaces factory Lower navigation/numpad and retains its media row. Semicolon/colon send P/Shift+P for host Colemak. Other unassigned Symbols positions inherit Base.\n\nNavigation (physical QWERTY positions): Y/O=line start/end (Ctrl+A/E; E sends physical K for Colemak); U/I=word left/right (Option+arrows); J/K/L/semicolon=Left/Down/Up/Right; P/slash=Page Up/Down; H also sends line end (Ctrl+E via physical K for host Colemak); N=Backspace; M=Command+Backspace (Meta+Backspace in Doom); period=Delete. Comma is reserved and disabled. Left-hand Navigation: W=Ctrl+Shift+Tab; E=Ctrl+Tab; R=held Ctrl+Option for Rectangle; A=Ctrl; S=Option; F=held Shift for selection; D and V reserved/disabled. R+arrows snaps windows; R+thumb Enter maximizes with Rectangle recommended shortcuts. Hold thumb Enter for Command and tap thumb Tab to cycle apps. Matching Doom Alt-arrow bindings provide word movement while Command remains Meta. Ctrl+A/E retain Doom's existing line-boundary commands.\n\nNumbers uses standard number keycodes: physical J/K/L=1/2/3, U/I/O=4/5/6, number-row 7/8/9 remain 7/8/9, comma (the comma/less-than key)=0, period=decimal point. M is reserved; N also gives 0. Magic (2) and Factory (3) retain factory mappings. Release typing-layer holds before using Magic because Navigation/Numbers have higher priority. See README for grids and import instructions.\n\nThe outer left key directly below Esc (original Grave position) is sticky Shift on Base (&sk LSHFT), using firmware defaults. Upper-left thumb remains dedicated Symbols; plain Backspace remains below it. Grave/backtick remains on Symbols physical P.",
